%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 161571b58ff05204dbb721f9b8e8c0a0, type: 3}
  m_Name: HavenPlaceVerbs
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: SafeHaven::HavenPlaceVerbs
  kinds:
  - kind: Wayfarer's Stones
    thoughts:
    - Four stones leaning together, worn smooth where hands rested on them. Travellers stopped here, once.
    - 'A line is cut into the tallest: a road, running toward the clearing. Toward the portal.'
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Island Stones
    thoughts:
    - Stones out in the water, set there on purpose. Whoever raised them wanted them hard to reach.
    - Moss on the landward side only. Whatever they were for, they faced the shore.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Drowned Stones
    thoughts:
    - Half of them under the water now. The lake has come up since they were set.
    - The water here is too still. Something about it makes me want to keep walking.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Fisher's Rest
    thoughts:
    - Old drying poles, and a fire-ring black with fish fat. They ate well here, for a while.
    - A net, rotted to strings on its pegs. Nobody came back for it.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Mother Maple
    thoughts:
    - The oldest tree I've seen this side of the portal. Its roots have swallowed a stone wall whole.
    - Scratches in the bark at head height, in rows. Someone was counting something, a long time ago.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Shepherd's Fold
    thoughts:
    - A ring of low walls for sheep. No sheep now; the grass has the place.
    - The gate faces the clearing. They brought the flock in toward the light at night.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Ruined Watchtower
    thoughts:
    - Someone watched the woods from here. The top has come down, but the stair still climbs.
    - Arrow-slits on the forest side only. They knew which way it would come from.
    lookout: 1
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Standing Stones
    thoughts:
    - A ring of standing stones, older than anything else out here. The carvings are worn almost flat.
    - Nothing grows inside the ring. Not moss, not grass.
    lookout: 1
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Lookout Cairn
    thoughts:
    - A cairn on the height, stacked by many hands, one stone at a time.
    - From up here the whole land lies open. Worth the climb.
    lookout: 1
    sound: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ae7d1e20fc649884f98a6aeaf01cfdb0, type: 2}
    soundWhen: 1
    soundEvery: {x: 18, y: 35}
  - kind: Old Barrow
    thoughts:
    - A long mound, grassed over, with a stone door in its side. A grave for someone who mattered.
    - The door was shut from the outside. And sealed again since, by someone else.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b088b17493cbde14da489f03fe9e5818, type: 2}
    soundWhen: 1
    soundEvery: {x: 10, y: 25}
  - kind: Burnt Farmstead
    thoughts:
    - The hearthstone is cracked right through. Somebody tried to keep this fire going after the roof was gone.
    - No bones. Whoever lived here walked away from it, or was taken.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b088b17493cbde14da489f03fe9e5818, type: 2}
    soundWhen: 1
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 28}
  - kind: Wolf Den
    thoughts:
    - A den under the rock-fall. The smell alone says keep back.
    - Gnawed bones at its mouth. Not all of them deer.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fd5c81c010255f543a1cc32216f4df89, type: 2}
    soundWhen: 2
    soundEvery: {x: 30, y: 60}
  - kind: Old Quarry
    thoughts:
    - Old cuttings in the rock, the marks of the wedges still in the stone. Masons worked here.
    - Some of the cut blocks were never carried away. As if they stopped in the middle of a day.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Elder Cedar
    thoughts:
    - A cedar older than the Haven. The air is cooler under it, and quiet.
    - 'Small things tucked into the bark: a bead, a twist of cloth. Offerings, or thanks.'
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Woodland Camp
    thoughts:
    - 'A camp in the trees: a fire-ring, a lean-to rotted down to its frame.'
    - They left in a hurry. The pot is still on its hook.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Grave in the Pines
    thoughts:
    - A cairn, a small one, with a stone at its head. Somebody put a hurdle round it to keep the animals off.
    - Whoever ran from the burning farm stopped here long enough to bury one of their own.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Old Steading
    thoughts:
    - A house's footing, a well, a yard fence half fallen. Nobody has drawn water here in a long time.
    - The old village reached further out than I thought. These were the hearth-keepers' farms.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Empty Hall
    thoughts:
    - A long hall's walls, knee-high now, and the long hearth down the middle. This is where they all sat at night.
    - An anvil by the door, the smith's logs still stacked. They didn't mean to come back.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Alder Spring
    thoughts:
    - A spring house of fieldstone and a step down to the water. The water has gone back into the ground.
    - Herbs were dried on that rack. Somebody here knew what grows by alders, and what it is good for.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Tarn Shrine
    thoughts:
    - Three stones above the tarn and a cairn behind them. The wind up here doesn't sound like wind.
    - Things were left here once, for the tarn. Whatever they asked of it, nobody remembers the answer.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  - kind: Sunken Causeway
    thoughts:
    - Boards laid across the fen, sinking one by one. Somebody tried to leave by the bog.
    - The causeway runs out into the mist and stops. So did whoever was walking it.
    lookout: 0
    sound: {fileID: 0}
    soundWhen: 0
    soundEvery: {x: 12, y: 25}
  finds:
